.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NQDCHUNK 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdchunk ,
.Nm nqdpiece
.Nd digests of the chunks of a large file, and a piece checked alone
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqdchunk
.Fa "const char *dir" "const char *path" "uint64_t chunk"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen" "char *why" "size_t wcap"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo nqdpiece
.Fa "const char *elem" "size_t n" "const char *piece" "uint64_t off"
.Fa "nqdrep **rep"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqdchunk
reads the file
.Fa path
in
.Fa dir
once and writes to
.Fa out
a
.Ql chunks
element
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5
in canonical JSON, for
.Xr nqdput 3 :
its path, its size, the chunk size
.Fa chunk
(1024 to 2^30 bytes) and the SHA-256 of each run of
.Fa chunk
bytes, the last run short.
The file is not split.
.Fa out
and
.Fa outlen
are as for
.Xr nqdjson 3 .
.Pp
.Fn nqdpiece
checks the file
.Fa piece ,
which holds the bytes of the element's file from byte
.Fa off
on (a multiple of the chunk size, at most the size), against the
.Ql chunks
element
.Fa elem
.Pf ( Fa n
bytes): each whole chunk in it, and a short last one when the piece ends
where the file does.
Only the piece is read.
The report's
.Ql chunk
rows name each chunk that differs, with its bytes (20 at most, then a
count), or say which chunks and bytes match; a short run at the end of a
piece that is not the end of the file is not checked, and a row says so.
.Pp
A capsule's seal covers the digests through its data record, so
.Xr nqchkx 3
with
.Fa only
set to
.Pa noqtis.data.json
checks them without the file.
.Xr nqdchk 3
checks each recorded file whole against its chunks.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn nqdchunk :
.Dv NQOK ;
.Dv NQEARG
for a chunk size out of bounds or a path a capsule cannot hold;
.Dv NQEIO
when the file cannot be read;
.Dv NQELIM
when the digests would not fit in a record (64 MiB: take larger chunks);
.Dv NQEBUF
for a
.Fa cap
too small.
.Pp
.Fn nqdpiece :
.Dv NQOK
when every chunk read matches and there was at least one (or the file is
empty);
.Dv NQEVRFY
otherwise, also for an element that is not valid;
.Fa *rep
is set in both cases
.Pq Xr nqdchk 3 .
.Dv NQEARG
for a
.Dv NULL
argument.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-chunk 1 ,
.Xr nqdchk 3 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
